[Music]  I've lived a life guided by completely  by desire in the sense that my guiding  principle as an artist has always been  to try to make the music that I most  wanted to hear so in listening to music  or looking at art I'm always thinking  two things I'm always thinking that's  great but actually it could be a bit  better if they had done this or that or  the other and a lot of the work that  I've made has come from the desire to  see something in existence that didn't  already exist it's it's never come  actually from the desire to make money  or to be famous though of the to the  latter is the more forgivable and I  think so I started to think what what is  desire for why have we evolved to have  desires because in fact we clearly do  respond to two types of signals one of  them is pain and pain tells us what to  avoid  but desire I think tells us what to go  for what to navigate towards now we like  sweetness for instance we we eat sweet  things why do we like sweet things we  like sweet things because sweetness is a  signal that something is at its maximum  vitamin value it's the right time for us  to eat it we like in my case attractive  women why do we do that because that  signal is saying that person is fertile  and you could multiply yourself with  that person  so romantic yes so so I'm thinking  desire is the is the sort of eudaimonic  reward it's the it's the thing that says  this is the right thing to be doing  so what interests me is what happens  when we virtualize our desires for  instance when I want sweetness now I  don't go and pick a cherry or an apple I  go and buy a Twix bar or something like  that what a Twix bar is it's the  sweetness without the benefits of the  sweetness it's the sweetness without the  vitamins that go with it we evolved that  desire for sweetness because it was a  way of improving ourselves essentially  physically improving ourselves so we can  now have sweetness without physically  improving ourselves in fact with making  ourselves quite a lot fatter we can now  have sex of a certain kind without  procreating so the thing that sex  evolved for has now been virtualized  into pornography or not necessarily  pornography heavy petting could be as  well essentially virtualization removes  us from the consequences of our  appetites and of course we now are a  newer stage of virtualization where we  have no virtue alized certain things  that used to be unvirtuous able such as  friendship we virtualized friendship by  having Facebook and Instagram and so on  we've we've managed to virtualize  activity we we were born with the need  to move around and with muscles that  want to stretch and so on and most of us  can't do that much of that so we go to  gyms or play football or whatever but  now we don't even do that we play  playstation so we have virtualized  activity we're running around but we're  not actually moving from our seat so  this is a new phase of human affairs I  think when and I think this it's  actually the answer to Fermi's paradox  do you know what Fermi's paradox is  Fermi's paradox is that if there are so  many stars in the universe and therefore  possibly so many habitable planets  and the number seems to go up every by a  power of 10 every few months why are we  not aware of any other civilizations why  does it just seem to be us and Geoffrey  West I think it was answered well of  course when we reach the stage when we  where we can virtualize all our  pleasures we stop trying to do anything  else outside in the world we can afford  to do everything inside the confines of  the box the TV set the computer so you  know most of the things that manifest  the existence of a civilization are the  result of that civilization trying to  broadcast something normally to its  other members but incidentally those  broadcasts would be heard elsewhere well  in a sense we've stopped broadcasting I  think and that to me is the sign that  we're at the end of the cycle I think  there may have been many many many other  civilizations that like us are being  killed by their own desire or have been  killed by them and on that cheerful note  my sister  [Applause]  to continue watching this video click  the link in the top left or in the  description below or visit a I dot TV  for more debates and talks from the  world's leading thinkers on today's  biggest ideas

